WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.890
I started to think of doing mathematics in
the one year before last of high school.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:14.179
So I was already 15 or something when I realized
that I was enjoying solving problems that

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:18.370
were resisting, that were a little harder
than usual.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:25.280
I had to think and absorb myself in them and
forget about everything else and come back

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.080
with a solution.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.020
One time I found a solution that was rather
creative.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:36.789
I remember the teacher was surprised when
I presented my solution, and I think this

00:00:36.789 --> 00:00:43.850
is when it really clicked for me that I would
like to try to do research in math, just because

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.040
I was enjoying the process.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.329
Indeed I don't see myself as a prodigy or
a genius at all.

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:57.300
There are geniuses out there, but the geniuses
are the exception rather than the norm — even

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.590
within the profession.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:04.040
Genius is kind of like a God-given thing,
right.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.800
You have it or you don't have it.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:13.620
I prefer to think of ability or talent, which
is something that can be cultivated and built

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.880
up with hard work.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.890
I think certainly you don't have to be a genius
to become a mathematician and to do interesting

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.030
mathematics.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:34.090
It's more a question of ability and having
the taste and the stamina to do it.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:42.450
Being wiling to put in the hard work and enjoying
the process of the research.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.280
Having the right frame of mind, the right
mindset for it.

